# Line endings for files that are executed or bind-mounted inside Linux
# containers.
#
# This repo has no .gitattributes history and `core.autocrlf=true` is the
# Windows default, so without these rules a Windows checkout hands coturn a
# turnserver.conf whose every value ends in a stray \r, and gen-cert.sh a
# shebang line that reads `#!/usr/bin/env sh\r` — both fail in ways that
# look like anything except a line-ending problem. Scoped by file type
# rather than by path so a new mounted config inherits it automatically.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
